  "method": "Time-weighted return: a value index is chain-linked between end-of-day (16:30 ET) valuation points, index_t = index_(t-1) * V_t / (V_(t-1) + external_flows); intra-day runs extend the index from the last EOD point. Teams have no external flows after Day 0 (Amendment 7), dividends/trades are internal. Period return = index_now / index_ref - 1 where ref = last EOD point before the period start (1d: previous session close; MTD/QTD/YTD: prior month/quarter/year end, or inception if later). 1y/3y/5y/10y are annualized and null until that much history exists; since_inception is always reported (cumulative). Benchmark uses ^SP500TR levels at the same reference points. See CONVENTIONS.md.",
